Package: agentknox
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: BoanLab @ Dankook University <namjh@dankook.ac.kr>
Homepage: https://github.com/boanlab/agentknox
Depends: libc6
Description: Transparent runtime security monitor and enforcer for AI coding agents
 AgentKnox monitors and enforces policy on AI coding agents (Claude Code,
 OpenAI Codex CLI, Crush, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot CLI) at the host kernel
 boundary using eBPF and BPF-LSM, without modifying the agents. It fuses the
 semantic layer (prompts, tool calls) with the system layer (files, processes,
 network) and enforces dual-layer policy in the kernel.
 .
 Runtime requirements: Linux x86-64, kernel 5.15+ with BTF, and 'bpf' in the
 active LSM list for in-kernel enforcement (otherwise it falls back to a
 userspace post-hoc enforcement backend). Installs and starts a systemd
 service; ships in observe-only mode until you add a policy under
 /etc/agentknox/policies.
